 ## Overview
-Automatic Differentiation (AD) for rendering computes the derivatives of interior rendering integrands by applying reverse-mode automatic differentiation directly to the rendering program [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently obtaining gradients for optimization-based inverse rendering by leveraging the fact that discretization commutes with differentiation for smooth interior integrands [S1]. Unlike the Adjoint Method, which derives custom adjoint equations for specific rendering paths, AD treats the renderer as a black-box computational graph, allowing the use of existing AD frameworks [S1].
