 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Memory Usage:** The computational graph for rendering is extremely large (millions of operations) and unstructured. Storing the forward tape for reverse AD can consume excessive memory, leading to out-of-memory errors [S1].
-- **Arithmetic Intensity:** Rendering operations often have low arithmetic intensity (e.g., many additions, few multiplications). This causes excessive memory traffic when data are repeatedly stored to and read back from memory buffers, making it significantly slower than high-intensity neural network operations [S1].
